<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE document SYSTEM "CommonMark.dtd">

<document xmlns="http://commonmark.org/xml/1.0">
  <thematic_break />
  <heading level="2">
    <text>id: uc-001 version: 1.0.0 status: draft created: 2026-08-05 updated: 2026-08-05</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="1">
    <text>Buy Goods</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Characteristic Information</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Goal in Context</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Buyer issues request directly to our company, expects goods shipped and to be billed.</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Scope</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Company (the system being designed as a black box)</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Level</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Summary</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Preconditions</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>We know Buyer (customer record exists in system)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>We know Buyer</text>
        <text>'</text>
        <text>s address</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer has valid contact information on file</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Success End Condition</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer has goods</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>We have money for the goods</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Order is recorded in system</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Invoice is sent to Buyer</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Failed End Condition</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>We have not sent the goods</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer has not spent the money</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Order is not recorded</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Primary Actor</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Buyer (any agent or computer acting for the customer)</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Secondary Actors</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Credit card company (for payment processing)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Bank (for payment processing)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Shipping service (for delivery)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Trigger</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Purchase request comes in (via phone, fax, web form, or electronic interchange)</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Frequency</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>200 per day</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Priority</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>Top</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Performance Target</text>
  </heading>
  <paragraph>
    <text>5 minutes for order, 45 days until paid</text>
  </paragraph>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Channels to Primary Actor</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Phone (interactive)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Fax (static file)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Web order form (interactive)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Electronic interchange (automated)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Channels to Secondary Actors</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Credit card company: interactive/API</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Bank: file/API</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Shipping service: file/API/timeout</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Related Use Cases</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Superordinate: Manage customer relationship (UC-002)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Subordinate: Create order (UC-015), Take payment by credit card (UC-044), Handle returned goods (UC-105)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Main Success Scenario</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="false" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer calls in with a purchase request.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company captures buyer</text>
        <text>'</text>
        <text>s name, address, requested goods, quantity, and delivery date preference.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company checks inventory for requested goods.</text>
      </paragraph>
      <paragraph>
        <text>This will use our trusty IBM OS/390 green screen application. Very fast</text>
        <text>!</text>
        <text>:</text>
      </paragraph>
      <list type="bullet" tight="true">
        <item>
          <paragraph>
            <text>Item 1</text>
          </paragraph>
        </item>
        <item>
          <paragraph>
            <text>Item 2</text>
          </paragraph>
        </item>
        <item>
          <paragraph>
            <text>Item 3</text>
          </paragraph>
        </item>
      </list>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company gives buyer information on goods, prices, delivery dates, and availability.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer confirms order details and signs for order.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company creates order in system.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company ships order to buyer.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company ships invoice to buyer.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer receives goods and verifies order.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer pays invoice.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company receives payment and records it.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Extensions</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 3a. Company is out of one of the ordered items</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company informs buyer of out-of-stock items.</text>
        <softbreak />
        <text>This should rarely happen. Still we have to address this.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer chooses to: (a) wait for restock, (b) substitute with similar item, or (c) remove item from order.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Return to step 4.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 4a. Buyer requests expedited shipping</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company calculates expedited shipping cost.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company provides expedited shipping quote to buyer.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer accepts or declines expedited shipping.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Return to step 5.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 5a. Buyer pays directly with credit card</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer provides credit card information.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company takes payment by credit card (UC-044).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Continue to step 6.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 7a. Shipping service is unavailable</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company attempts to use backup shipping service.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>If backup service also unavailable, company informs buyer of delay.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company retries shipping when service becomes available.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 8a. Invoice delivery fails</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company retries invoice delivery via alternate channel (email, fax, mail).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>If all channels fail, company logs issue for manual follow-up.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 10a. Buyer returns goods</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer initiates return request.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company handles returned goods (UC-105).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company processes refund or credit.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 10b. Buyer disputes charge</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company initiates dispute resolution process.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company provides documentation to buyer.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Dispute is resolved (refund, credit, or confirmation of charge).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Extension 10c. Payment fails</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="ordered" start="1" tight="true" delimiter="period">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Company retries payment collection.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>If retry fails, company contacts buyer to resolve payment issue.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Once payment is received, continue to step 11.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Sub-Variations</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Step 1: Buyer may use</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Phone call</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Fax</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Web order form</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Electronic data interchange (EDI)</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Step 2: Company may capture information via</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Manual entry by customer service representative</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Automated web form</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>EDI system</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Step 7: Company may ship via</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Standard ground shipping</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Expedited shipping</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Overnight shipping</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Local pickup</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Step 10: Buyer may pay via</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Cash or money order</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Check</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Credit card</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Debit card</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Bank transfer</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Digital wallet</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Open Issues</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>What happens if we have only part of the order in stock?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>What happens if credit card is stolen?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>What is the maximum wait time for out-of-stock items before order is cancelled?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>How do we handle international orders?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>What is the refund policy for returned goods?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>How do we handle partial payments?</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <text>Related Information</text>
  </heading>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Notes</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>This is a high-level summary use case that encompasses multiple lower-level use cases (UC-015, UC-044, UC-105).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>The main success scenario represents the </text>
        <text>&quot;</text>
        <text>happy path</text>
        <text>&quot;</text>
        <text> with minimal exceptions.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Extensions represent alternative flows that still result in successful order completion.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Sub-variations represent different technologies or methods for accomplishing the same step.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
  <heading level="3">
    <text>Assumptions</text>
  </heading>
  <list type="bullet" tight="true">
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Buyer has already been authenticated and verified.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>System has access to real-time inventory data.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Payment processing is handled by external services (credit card company, bank).</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
    <item>
      <paragraph>
        <text>Shipping is handled by external shipping service.</text>
      </paragraph>
    </item>
  </list>
</document>
